WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.201
Hi, I'm Bowsprit!

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:06.149
Cua Spaces gives an agent its own desktop on a computer you own.

00:00:09.017 --> 00:00:13.060
The idea: every computer runs one small daemon, and any agent reaches

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.745
it through the same SDK.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.639
Your agent, say Claude Code, calls the cua SDK.

00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:24.858
The Space's id picks the path: an address and a token, or the relay.

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:30.492
Inside the computer, one daemon answers: shell, files, screenshots, windows and video.

00:00:30.912 --> 00:00:33.004
It never moves the mouse itself.

00:00:33.004 --> 00:00:35.793
Input goes through cua driver, linked right in.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:40.378
To start an agent in a Space, the SDK does four things.

00:00:40.798 --> 00:00:42.743
Install the harness, pinned and checked.

00:00:43.284 --> 00:00:45.630
Write the run as files in the guest, so any client

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.483
can pick it up.

00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:49.420
Drive the harness over the agent client protocol.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:51.493
And give it the Space's own tools.

00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:56.958
On the relay's web path, encryption ends at the relay, so it

00:00:56.958 --> 00:00:58.005
can read the session.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.989
The default mesh encrypts end to end.

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.773
The relay only forwards ciphertext.

00:01:04.758 --> 00:01:07.908
I ran the daemon on a virtual desktop and drove it from

00:01:07.908 --> 00:01:09.483
a script: type, then press save.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.466
Reading the window again showed exactly the change.

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:17.761
Every click took over a second, mostly the driver watching for a dialog.

00:01:17.761 --> 00:01:19.850
Cut that watch and the click halves.

00:01:21.258 --> 00:01:24.647
Each Space is its own connection, so jobs on all of

00:01:24.647 --> 00:01:25.880
them overlap almost completely.

00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:29.656
The takeaway: Cua stopped owning the agent.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.482
Whichever agent you already use drives the computer.

00:01:35.108 --> 00:01:36.359
One daemon per computer.

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:36.985
Any agent.

00:01:36.985 --> 00:01:38.861
And a click is mostly waiting.

00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:41.835
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:42.443
I'm Bowsprit.

00:01:42.443 --> 00:01:42.747
Bye!
